+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Feature Branch**: n/a (main) | **Created**: 2026-11-11 | **Status**: Draft
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Quote a rental (P1)
+Desk staff register boards and sails, then ask what renting one costs for a period.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a board at 2500 cents/day, when quoting 2026-05-01T00:00:00Z → 2026-05-04T00:00:00Z (3 days), then total is 7500.
+2. Given an unknown item, or a period that is not whole UTC days, empty or reversed, then the quote is refused with an error.
+
+### User Story 2 - Book a rental (P1)
+Desk staff book an item for a period; the booking gets an identifier and the quoted total.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a free item, when booked, then a booking `{id, itemId, start, end, total}` is returned with a unique id.
+2. Given an existing booking, when another overlaps it on the same item, then the booking is refused.
+3. Back-to-back periods (end of one = start of next) do not overlap; other items are unaffected.
+4. A refused booking leaves no trace.
+
+### Edge cases
+- Duplicate equipment id, invalid kind, or non-integer / negative dailyPrice are rejected.
+- Unparseable dates, or dates not written as UTC ISO-8601, are rejected.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `createRentalService()` is exported from `src/index.ts`, in-memory only.
+- **FR-002**: `addEquipment({id, kind, dailyPrice})` with kind `board` or `sail`; dailyPrice is integer euro cents (rule 1).
+- **FR-003**: `quote({itemId,start,end})` returns `{itemId,start,end,total}`, total = days × dailyPrice.
+- **FR-004**: `book(request)` returns `{id,itemId,start,end,total}`.
+- **FR-005**: Times are UTC ISO-8601; start and end must be midnight UTC with end after start (rules 2, 3).
+- **FR-006**: quote/book throw for unknown item or disallowed period; book also throws when the item is not free for the whole period (rule 4).
+- **FR-007**: Cancellation (rule 5) is out of scope now; the data kept per booking must allow it later (start, total, id).
+
+## Key Entities
+Equipment (id, kind, dailyPrice); Booking (id, itemId, start, end, total).
+
+## Success Criteria
+- SC-001: Every quote and booking total is an exact integer number of cents.
+- SC-002: No two bookings of one item ever overlap.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Returned start/end are the request strings as given (canonical form accepted: `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z` or `...T00:00:00Z`).
+- Constitution is an unfilled template; the five school rules are the governing constraints.
